        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The cat and the box"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The cat jumped quickly into the box and slept under the lid.\n\"Find the action, the how and the where,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "verb",
          "adverb",
          "preposition",
          "auxiliary verb"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A verb shows action or state: jumped, slept, is. An adverb tells how, when or where about a verb: quickly. A preposition shows the link between a noun and another word: into, under, on, between.\nMain verbs can have helpers called auxiliary verbs: is, are, was, has, will. In She has finished, has helps finished.\nA preposition comes before a noun or pronoun: in the box, on the table, between two trees."
        }
